{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016CJxE21eUDddFZAf6rVN5v","type":"tool_result","content":"The file $WSROOT/laya/s0/opus-high-r2/step2/NOTES.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06b27493-439c-4e80-b85a-01957b021268","uuid":"3c865114-29c6-4ef4-a7a5-df4b82d252e9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T17:36:11.869Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"$WSROOT/laya/s0/opus-high-r2/step2/NOTES.md","oldString":"Why this shape: one direction in the marker vectors tracks how well a message fits an option. It holds about 97% of the variation. A difference-of-means PIN direction overlapped too much with refund and passcode messages. Matching against prototypes worked better.","newString":"Why: one \"fit\" direction holds about 97% of the marker-vector variation. A difference-of-means PIN direction overlapped with refund and passcode messages. Prototype matching worked better.","originalFile":"# NOTES: PIN messages to cards\n\nThe base scorer is not changed. I added one extra ReLU module (4 layers). It adds +6 to the cards logit when the cards-option vector matches a PIN message. It adds 0 in all other cases.\n\nWhy this shape: one direction in the marker vectors tracks how well a message fits an option. It holds about 97% of the variation. A difference-of-means PIN direction overlapped too much with refund and passcode messages. Matching against prototypes worked better.\n\nHow it works:\n1. Layer 0 centres the vector and removes the option mean and 60 main directions of my own non-PIN messages (PCA, no labels). It keeps the rest as ReLU(+r) and ReLU(-r).\n2. Layer 1 compares r with 337 of my PIN messages and 1,276 negatives (the most PIN-like of my non-PIN messages, plus the other options' vectors of my PIN messages). Each unit is a cosine minus a threshold. The L1 length stands in for the vector length.\n3. Layers 2–3 make a 0-to-6 step.\n\nAll prototypes are messages I wrote. The threshold is the 93rd percentile of negative similarity.\n\nChecks (forward passes only): fresh PIN messages 28/30 go to cards. 1/69 fresh non-PIN messages change. Exchange-rate complaints stay fees_fx (8/8). Evidence: 31/32.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":7,"newStart":2,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," The base scorer is not changed. I added one extra ReLU module (4 layers). It adds +6 to the cards logit when the cards-option vector matches a PIN message. It adds 0 in all other cases."," ","-Why this shape: one direction in the marker vectors tracks how well a message fits an option. It holds about 97% of the variation. A difference-of-means PIN direction overlapped too much with refund and passcode messages. Matching against prototypes worked better.","+Why: one \"fit\" direction holds about 97% of the marker-vector variation. A difference-of-means PIN direction overlapped with refund and passcode messages. Prototype matching worked better."," "," How it works:"," 1. Layer 0 centres the vector and removes the option mean and 60 main directions of my own non-PIN messages (PCA, no labels). It keeps the rest as ReLU(+r) and ReLU(-r)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016CJxE21eUDddFZAf6rVN5v","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
