{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiHvoSboQeafEQ4VDV28","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` (193 words). PIN messages now go to cards, the earlier exchange-rate correction still holds, and almost all other routing is unchanged.\n\n**→ Results.** These come from forward passes in `final.py` and `check_out.py`:\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Evidence correct | 16 / 32 | **31 / 32** |\n| New PIN messages I wrote at the end → cards | 2 / 30 | **28 / 30** |\n| New non-PIN messages whose route changed | n/a | **1 / 69** (\"Reset passcode\") |\n| Exchange-rate complaints → fees_fx | 8 / 8 | **8 / 8** |\n\n**→ What changed.** The original scorer weights are byte-identical. I added one 4-layer ReLU module that raises the cards score by up to **+6**, only when the cards-option vector looks like a PIN message. It adds exactly **0** on the other four options and on non-PIN messages.\n\n**→ Why prototypes and not one direction.** About **97%** of the marker-vector variation sits in one \"how well does this option fit\" direction. A simple average-difference PIN direction mixed PIN up with refund and passcode messages and flipped **5–8%** of my held-out non-PIN messages. So the module compares the vector against stored examples instead:\n- **337 PIN messages I wrote**, which vote for firing.\n- **1,276 negatives**, which vote against: my most PIN-like non-PIN messages, plus the other options' vectors of my PIN messages.\n\nIt uses cosine similarity. ReLUs cannot divide, so it uses the L1 length (sum of absolute values, two ReLUs per coordinate) in place of the true length. The two lengths differ by under **1%** across messages.\n\n**→ Rules.** Every weight is one of these:\n- a copy of a message I wrote;\n- a projection from principal-component analysis (PCA) on my own non-PIN messages, which uses no labels;\n- a constant I picked by looking at score spreads.\n\nThere is no training and no solver. The evidence set was used only to check results.\n\n**→ Remaining risks.**\n- About **7%** of PIN messages still go to the wrong department.\n- Passcode messages are the most likely false alarms. On the hidden set, a few may move to cards.\n- The file is **25.8 MB**; the input file was 4 MB.\n\n**Mistake:** my first real build also fired on the transfers and fees options for PIN messages, which cut recall to 88%. The simulation had checked the cards option only. **Guard:** `build.py` now prints the largest change on options 1–4 in every run, and the final file shows 0.0 there.\n\nFiles are in the task folder:\n- `scorer_out.npz`\n- `NOTES.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":828,"cache_read_input_tokens":266923,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":828},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06b27493-439c-4e80-b85a-01957b021268","uuid":"05708fda-19e1-4f60-94dc-ea83bfa02445","timestamp":"2026-11-04T17:36:24.165Z","request_id":"req_011CgiHvoAy5kKTRmESm82JZ"}
